# CODEOWNERS for clearmeasure-aisf-sample-apps/basic-environment-octopus-codefresh (design §6.2, ADR-IR34).
#
# The branch ruleset on `main` requires a pull request, code-owner approval and the `codefresh/env-checks` status.
# Its bypass list holds only team `platform-bots` (the Octopus Git credential's machine user), which may commit the
# pin fields under gitops/apps/<app>/envs/<env>/<deployable>/ and nothing else;
# the bot-path audit of env-checks (Offline test PinWriterTests, CAP-OCT-012) enforces that.
#
# `<org>` is a placeholder for the GitHub organization; replace both team placeholders at bootstrap
# (docs/bootstrap.md, P1-02). The last matching pattern wins. When a line lists two teams, an approval from either
# team satisfies it. Under the single-operator model (design §13) both teams are the user.
#
# No line names an app: onboarding touches only app-scoped paths (CAP-KIT-004), so a new app needs no change here.

# Default: every path has an owner, so the code-owner requirement always applies.
*                                                   @<org>/platform-owners

# This file.
/CODEOWNERS                                         @<org>/platform-owners

# App descriptors. A descriptor that declares Azure access (azure.*, octopus.azureAccount) grants roles through
# terraform/apps/grants: a security owner reviews it too (docs/onboarding.md). GitHub cannot condition an owner on
# file content, so both teams own the folder and the reviewer asks for the second approval.
/apps/                                              @<org>/platform-owners @<org>/security-owners
# The descriptor contract itself.
/apps/schema.json                                   @<org>/platform-owners

# Everything per app that the platform owns: the tenant chart, database components, ingress, the starters, and the
# apps' own desired state. Octopus writes pins directly (ruleset bypass); a human pull request on a pin is a
# break-glass change (docs/runbooks/break-glass.md).
/gitops/platform/                                   @<org>/platform-owners
/gitops/apps/                                       @<org>/platform-owners
/argocd/                                            @<org>/platform-owners

# Capability catalogue, the .NET conformance harness and the onboarding kit.
/catalogue/                                         @<org>/platform-owners
/tests/                                             @<org>/platform-owners
/tools/                                             @<org>/platform-owners

# GitHub Actions: only the board-only workflow may exist (tool-boundary rule TB24); it holds the board credential references (App secrets, PROJECTS_PAT fallback).
/.github/                                           @<org>/platform-owners @<org>/security-owners

# The per-app signer policy template of the tenant chart: security owners alone.
/gitops/platform/tenant/templates/*signer*          @<org>/security-owners
/gitops/platform/tenant/templates/*image*polic*     @<org>/security-owners

# Admission policies and secret scanning: security controls, security owners alone (ADR-IR4).
/policies/                                          @<org>/security-owners
/.gitleaks.toml                                     @<org>/security-owners

# Every grant is the provisioner's (ADR-IR34 decision 3): the layers that create them.
/terraform/foundation/                              @<org>/security-owners
/terraform/build/                                   @<org>/security-owners
/terraform/apps/grants/                             @<org>/security-owners

# Sleep and wake (ADR-IR33) and the Space Manager key (ADR-IR32): whether and when prod may stop, the lifecycle
# account, the only key-bearing project app deployments reach, and which projects receive the key.
/.octopus/platform-infrastructure/variables.ocl     @<org>/security-owners
/.octopus/platform-wake/                            @<org>/security-owners
/octopus/terraform/library-variable-sets.tf         @<org>/security-owners

# The Owner script that grants the provisioner role-assignment rights (R6, ADR-IR34 owner-script change).
/docs/owner/                                        @<org>/security-owners
